The following were ported from it to Rust, with modifications (each ported file carries an attribution
header naming its origin):

- the semantic compilation pipeline: auto_ontology/semantic/pipeline.py, compile.py, visit_enter.py,
  cancellation.py (the ordered commit queue, per-table processing, column profiling, cancellation);
- deterministic column mapping, foreign-key suggestion and term extraction: auto_ontology/semantic/
  deterministic.py, fk_suggester.py, term_extractor.py, models.py, domain.py;
- semantic foreign-key resolution: auto_ontology/semantic/semantic_fk.py;
- bridge (junction) tables and SqlAttribute suggestion: auto_ontology/semantic/bridge_tables.py,
  sql_attribute_suggester.py;
- date-format inference and the embedding texts: auto_ontology/semantic/date_format.py, embed.py;
- catalog ingestion: auto_ontology/catalog/extract.py, normalize.py, table_filter.py, diff.py, sql_parse.py,
  query_stats.py, parsers/sqlglot_extractor.py, parsers/query_comparator.py, model/query.py;
- the model prompts (reproduced verbatim in src/prompts.rs);
- the intent of the upstream unit tests (semantic/tests, catalog/tests), rewritten as Rust tests.

NVIDIA Auto Ontology's own notice reads: "This distribution includes open source which is archived at the
following URL: https://opensource.nvidia.com/oss/teams/nvidia".

Changes made in this port: rewritten in Rust; SQL parsing on the `sqlparser` crate instead of sqlglot; the
catalog snapshot and query log arrive over an HTTP API from Cairn instead of being read by connectors; values
are sampled by Cairn under its governance instead of by the compiler; relationships also come from joins
observed in the query log; usage ranking uses the documented fix of the upstream scorer; the ontology is stored
in PostgreSQL (or SQLite) with versioned compilation runs; SQL validation and graph exports were added.
